=== CI FAILURE ROOT-CAUSE FINDING: PR #93's first push failed delivery-activation/rccad-methodology/validation-closure with ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'spikes' ===
Root cause: this file's own module-level imports relied on ANOTHER test module's sys.path.insert(0, REPOSITORY_ROOT) side effect having already run in the same pytest session (an established but undocumented cross-file dependency several existing task test files rely on). ocor-runtime/tests/mission_thread/ sorts alphabetically BEFORE ocor-runtime/tests/tasks/, so when the whole suite is collected in one pytest invocation, this new file is imported before any tasks/test_ocor_dev_XXXX.py file's sys.path.insert has executed. Local testing had masked this because 'python -m pytest' (used locally) auto-prepends the CWD to sys.path, unlike the bare 'pytest' console script CI invokes via 'uv run --project ocor-runtime --frozen pytest'.
Fix: added this file's own explicit sys.path.insert(0, REPOSITORY_ROOT), matching the established, collection-order-independent pattern already used by test_ocor_dev_0004/0015/0016/0017/0018/0021/0024/0025/0029/0079/0082/0083/0084.py.

